node_modules/
*.log
.env

# Local-only Claude/impeccable state
.claude/settings.local.json
.impeccable/
PRODUCT.md
# The impeccable skill installs a full copy of itself into all three of these.
# This repo publishes a plugin to a marketplace: a stray `git add -A` would
# vendor ~50 files of someone else's skill into it. Ignored, not deleted.
.claude/skills/
.github/skills/
.github/hooks/
test-fixtures/**/out/
# Ideation working artifacts stay local — but the learning store is meant to be
# committed and shared, so it is explicitly un-ignored. (`docs/ideation/*` not
# `docs/ideation/`: git cannot re-include a file under an ignored directory.)
docs/ideation/*
!docs/ideation/learnings.md

# The root package.json declares pi-extension dependencies (pi-subagents,
# pi-dynamic-workflows, rpiv-ask-user-question) so a single `pi install` brings
# them in. package-lock.json is committed to pin the floating ^ ranges — pi's
# git-clone install runs `npm install`, which respects the lockfile for
# reproducible installs. CI uses `node --run test`, which never loads the
# extensions. Leading slash on purpose: `site/pnpm-lock.yaml` is real and
# tracked, and a bare pattern would swallow it.
/pnpm-lock.yaml

# Astro site build output and cache (the site is built by Cloudflare from source)
site/dist/
site/.astro/
site/.wrangler/
